<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stadacona</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stadacona was a St Lawrence Iroquoian village on the site of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/quebec">Quebec</a> City, visited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-cartier">Jacques Cartier</a> in 1535. Its chief Donnacona traded with the French, and Cartier wintered nearby in 1535–1536 before taking Donnacona to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The village had vanished by the time <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samuel-de-champlain">Samuel de Champlain</a> founded Quebec in 1608.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stadacona.jpg" alt="Stadacona" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marc-Aurèle de Foy Suzor-Coté · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacques_Cartier_Meeting_the_Indians_at_Stadacona,_1535.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
